# Generated catalogue artifacts — never hand-merge these.
#
# index-fragment.json and artifacts/*.json are produced deterministically by
# scripts/build_fragment.py (the "Build catalogue" CI workflow) from this repo's
# apps/<id>/manifest.json. They MUST be committed (served raw via GitHub Pages),
# so they can't be .gitignored — but a hand-merge of their conflict markers is
# never correct. (This extended repo has NO catalogue.json — the base repo owns
# the merged catalogue.)
#
# The "ours" merge driver auto-resolves any merge/rebase conflict in these files
# to the current side (no conflict markers); CI then regenerates the
# authoritative content on the next apps/ push. If you need the local copy exact
# after an auto-resolved merge, just run:
#     py scripts/build_fragment.py --source ext1
#
# REQUIRES a one-time, per-clone config — the driver command lives in
# .git/config, which git does NOT track:
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
# Without it, git falls back to a normal text merge and the conflicts return.
index-fragment.json merge=ours linguist-generated=true
artifacts/*.json    merge=ours linguist-generated=true
